      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To determine the extent and severity of obesity-related cardiorespiratory morbidity in children with body mass index (BMI) >or=40 kg/m(2)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "STUDY DESIGN",
          "content": "Cross-sectional analysis of a cohort comprised of 48 boys and girls aged 8 to 17 years with BMI >or=40 kg/m(2). Cardiorespiratory fitness (graded cycle exercise test), left ventricular (LV) mass (echocardiography), blood pressure, fasting lipid profile, fasting insulin, fasting glucose, HbA1c, and pulmonary function (spirometry and sleep studies) were measured."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The cohort averaged 14.2 +/- 2 years of age with mean BMI of 45.5 kg/m(2). Only 2 patients had normal fitness; 37 of 48 had peak oxygen consumption <20 mL O(2)/minute. Hypertension was present in 10 of 48 patients. Mean lipid values were: triglycerides 103 +/- 48 mg/dL, HDL cholesterol 41 +/- 10 mg/dL, and LDL cholesterol 108 +/- 26 mg/dL. Type II diabetes mellitus was diagnosed in 6 patients. Mean fasting insulin was 31 +/- 19 microU/mL. Asthma treatment, small airways disease by pulmonary function testing, or both were present in 35 of 48 patients; upper airway obstruction was present in 7 patients. LV hypertrophy was present in 8 patients, with a mean LV mass of 43 +/- 11 g/m(2.7)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Children and adolescents with BMI >or=40 kg/m(2) have substantial cardiorespiratory morbidity including severe physical deconditioning."
        }
      ]},
